;;; M1a S1a.6.6 — a premise whose relation head is an unbound variable.
;;;
;;; `(?R ?x)` in a `:match` needs `?R` bound by the rule's activator (Q29 —
;;; M1 matches relations per activator). Here the rule declares one parameter
;;; `(?S)` and the activator `(uses-free-head p)` binds it, so `?R` is free
;;; and the compiler rejects the rule. The run exits 1 with the message on
;;; one stderr line, after the error's class path:
;;;
;;;     ein.inference.compile.CompileError: unbound relation head ?R …
;;;
;;; **Refused at load since M1e2 S1e2.2.24** (W24, the stage file's default
;;; 1): the loader reads a relation variable no parameter binds as it reads
;;; the same shape inside a pattern, and every command that loads the file
;;; exits 1, as before, with *kb load error: rule 'uses-free-head': its
;;; :match writes (?R ?x) with ?R as its relation, which no parameter binds —
;;; a relation is named by a name or by a parameter its activator binds*
;;; where the `CompileError` above stood.
;;;
;;; A refusal rather than an answer, so what pins it is the corpus sweep's
;;; banked golden — exit code and stderr. Found by the S1a.6.6 fuzzer's
;;; mutation arm, minimised to two forms.

(rule uses-free-head (?S)
  :match  (?R ?x)
  :assert (p ?x) :why "{?x} is in some relation ?R that no parameter binds, so p holds of {?x}")

(uses-free-head p)
